riaandeJongh","html_url":"https://github.com/AdriaandeJongh","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdriaandeJongh/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdriaandeJongh/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdriaandeJongh/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdriaandeJongh/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdriaandeJongh/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdriaandeJongh/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdriaandeJongh/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdriaandeJongh/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdriaandeJongh/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"With this PR on macOS 26.4.1, using:\r\n```\r\nfunc _input(event: InputEvent) -> void:\r\n\tif event is InputEventJoypadButton:\r\n\t\tvar iejb: InputEventJoypadButton = event\r\n\t\tprint(Input.get_joy_info(iejb.device))\r\n\t\tprint(Input.get_joy_name(iejb.device))\r\n```\r\n\r\nMicrosoft Xbox One Wireless Controller: \r\n```\r\n{ \"raw_name\": \"Controller\", \"vendor_id\": \"1118\", \"product_id\": \"736\" }\r\nController\r\n```\r\n\r\nSony Playstation 4 Wireless Controller:\r\n```\r\n{ \"raw_name\": \"PS4 Controller\", \"vendor_id\": \"1356\", \"product_id\": \"1476\"}\r\nPS4 Controller\r\n```\r\n\r\n8BitDo Pro Controller:\r\n```\r\n{ \"raw_name\": \"8BitDo Pro 3\", \"vendor_id\": \"1452\", \"product_id\": \"4\" }\r\n8BitDo Pro 3\r\n```\r\n\r\nSo it looks like the Xbox controller returns a generic name with this change and that could be considered a regression. However, with the vendor_id and product_id, is it possible to deduce that this is an Xbox controller anyway?","created_at":"2026-05-01T08:28:36Z","updated_at":"2026-05-01T08:28:36Z","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119024#discussion_r3172601920","pull_request_url":"https://api.gith